---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About">
  <header class="article-head"><h1>About this journal</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Most of what's written about AI is about models and chips. This journal is about one thing underneath them: power for AI data centres. It follows one question across seven chapters, from the grid connection to the transformers, the turbines, solar and batteries, and finally the reactors. At each step I ask the same thing: what decides whether the power turns up on time?</p>
    <p>This layer is where the physics is slow, the data is public and the constraint is real. It's also the part almost nobody explains in plain English.</p>
    <p>Every piece starts with a one-line version anyone can follow, then goes as deep as it needs to. Where I have a view, I say what would prove me wrong. The plain English comes first. After that there's a section for investors on the same page, with the numbers, the claims I've put on record and what would prove them wrong.</p>
    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>I'm {SITE.author}. I trained as a civil engineer (UCL MEng, 2025) and then moved into investment research. I was an Investment Analyst at Cross Labs / Cross Compass in Tokyo, and now I run this journal as Founder and Research Analyst, The Physical Layer, publishing research on power for AI data centres.</p>
    <p>Engineering taught me to respect what has to be physically true. Research taught me to say what I think will happen, and what would prove me wrong. This journal is where I put the two together.</p>
    <p class="sources">Everything here is personal research, not investment advice. Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or on <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
